      "title": "Evaluating Hydrogen Fuel Cell Vehicles",
      "prompt": "A car manufacturer markets a new hydrogen fuel cell vehicle as producing 'zero emissions.' An environmental scientist is asked to evaluate this marketing claim. (a) Describe what actually occurs at the point of use in a hydrogen fuel cell vehicle, and evaluate whether the 'zero emissions' claim is accurate at this specific stage. (b) Explain what additional information would be needed to evaluate whether the vehicle is genuinely 'zero emissions' across its full life cycle. (c) Describe two different hydrogen production scenarios — one that would support a stronger overall 'clean' claim, and one that would undermine it.",
