      "prompt": "A city located in a mountain valley reports its worst air quality readings occur during winter mornings following clear, calm nights, with ground-level ozone remaining low during these events but particulate matter and carbon monoxide reaching hazardous levels. (a) Identify the atmospheric phenomenon most likely responsible for this pattern and explain the mechanism. (b) Explain why ground-level ozone remains low during these specific events, even though other pollutants spike. (c) Propose one specific intervention the city could implement to reduce the severity of these events.",
